{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 11 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.util.Scanner;\nimport java.util.TreeMap;\n\npublic class Problems {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = sc.nextInt();\n        int B = sc.nextInt();\n        int[] arr = new int[n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {\n            arr[i] = sc.nextInt();\n        }\n\n        TreeMap<Integer, Integer> buckets = new TreeMap<>();\n        int sum = 0;\n\n        int evens = 0;\n        int odds = 0;\n        int start = 0;\n        int count = 0;\n        int k = 1;\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < arr.length - 1; i++) {\n            if (arr[i] % 2 == 0) {\n                evens++;\n            } else {\n                odds++;\n            }\n\n            if (evens == odds) {\n                int diff = Math.abs(arr[i + 1] - arr[i]);\n                int max = bucketMax(buckets);\n                if (sum > B && diff < max) {\n                    sum -= max;\n                    buckets.put(max, buckets.get(max) - 1);\n                    if (buckets.get(max) == 0) buckets.remove(max);\n                    buckets.put(diff, buckets.getOrDefault(diff, 0) + 1);\n                    sum += diff;\n                } else if (sum < B) {\n                    sum += diff;\n                    buckets.put(diff, buckets.getOrDefault(diff, 0) + 1);\n                    count++;\n                    start = i + 1;\n                }\n                if (i == arr.length - 2 && k < arr.length - 1) {\n                    i = start++;\n                    evens = odds = 0;\n                }\n            }\n\n        }\n        while (sum > B) {\n            int maxKey = buckets.lastKey();\n            if (buckets.get(maxKey) > 0) {\n                sum -= maxKey;\n                count--;\n                buckets.put(maxKey, buckets.get(maxKey) - 1);\n                if (buckets.get(maxKey) == 0) buckets.remove(maxKey);\n            }\n        }\n\n        System.out.println(count);\n    }\n\n    private static int bucketMax(TreeMap<Integer, Integer> buckets) {\n        if (buckets.isEmpty()) return -1;\n        return buckets.lastKey();\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nimport heapq\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    it = iter(data)\n    n = int(next(it))\n    B = int(next(it))\n    arr = [int(next(it)) for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # buckets: dict for counts, max_heap for negative diffs (max-heap)\n    counts = {}\n    max_heap = []\n\n    def get_max_key():\n        # clean heap and return current max key, or -1 if empty\n        while max_heap and counts.get(-max_heap[0], 0) == 0:\n            heapq.heappop(max_heap)\n        if max_heap:\n            return -max_heap[0]\n        return -1\n\n    sum_diff = 0\n    evens = 0\n    odds = 0\n    start = 0\n    count = 0\n    k = 1  # constant, used only in reset condition\n\n    i = 0\n    while i < n - 1:\n        # process arr[i]\n        if arr[i] % 2 == 0:\n            evens += 1\n        else:\n            odds += 1\n\n        if evens == odds:\n            diff = abs(arr[i + 1] - arr[i])\n            max_key = get_max_key()\n            if sum_diff > B and diff < max_key:\n                # remove max_key\n                sum_diff -= max_key\n                counts[max_key] -= 1\n                if counts[max_key] == 0:\n                    del counts[max_key]\n                # add diff\n                counts[diff] = counts.get(diff, 0) + 1\n                sum_diff += diff\n                heapq.heappush(max_heap, -diff)\n            elif sum_diff < B:\n                sum_diff += diff\n                counts[diff] = counts.get(diff, 0) + 1\n                heapq.heappush(max_heap, -diff)\n                count += 1\n                start = i + 1\n\n        # reset logic (original for loop's reset at end of iteration)\n        if i == n - 2 and k < n - 1:\n            i = start\n            start += 1\n            evens = 0\n            odds = 0\n            # after reset, we will increment i at the end of loop\n        else:\n            i += 1\n\n    # remove largest diffs while sum > B\n    while sum_diff > B:\n        max_key = get_max_key()\n        if max_key == -1:\n            break  # should not happen\n        sum_diff -= max_key\n        count -= 1\n        counts[max_key] -= 1\n        if counts[max_key] == 0:\n            del counts[max_key]\n\n    print(count)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-7.510157047363464e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -0.000161038784426637, -0.0019558602944016457, -0.00026127262390218675, -0.00020895205670967698, -3.576278118089249e-07, -4.768258077092469e-05, -0.00013302871957421303, -3.4689302992774174e-05, -0.6396964192390442, -0.0009120118920691311, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.0009171332349069417, 0.0, -0.0024801704566925764, 0.0, -1.9788545614574105e-05, 